WEBVTT

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.910
This is footage from right before the 
Times Square ceremony began.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.870
The time is...

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.310
8:03.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.500
Could that be Wraith?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.820
I don't know.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.570
Huh?

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.550
Anything else?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.710
On the day of the Times Square incident,

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.640
a lot of other things happened 
in New York, too...

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.670
But this caught my attention.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.790
A 28-year-old boutique employee 
named Jennifer Allen disappeared.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.390
That's not all.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:48.800
Two days before,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.150
her cousin May, a student from 
Dayton, Ohio, also disappeared.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.500
The last person who saw Jennifer

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.170
was her roommate, who said she left for work

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.690
at around 8:30 AM.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.740
I thought it might be close...

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.550
Sorry.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.330
I guess this basically means that 
I wasn't able to find anything.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.970
But something's on your mind, right?

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.360
A security camera in Dayton...

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.730
I think it was two mornings ago.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.830
There.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.110
Could you follow this lead?

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.010
Ow, hot!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.340
Huh?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.180
Huh? Wait...

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.930
I'm sorry. I...

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:44.940
Someone!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.900
Someone, help! My child is still in there!

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.670
Joey!

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.190
Dayton...

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.120
You're going to Dayton, where the 
second person went missing, right?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.820
I'm going, too.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.200
This is the work of that woman who uses fire.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.220
Since they're coming after you,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.680
you must've learned something 
they didn't want getting out.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.450
But if you don't want to die, 
you should hide somewhere.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.550
There's nowhere that I can!

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.290
I have nowhere to go.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.310
Do you have a car?

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.330
I'm feeling better.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.130
I have a lot more appetite than before.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.050
It's a bit bothersome, actually.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.580
Nothing has really changed.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.000
The days just peacefully 
pass by before I know it.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.380
Hmm...

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.290
Oh, yeah.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.190
I had a dream that I couldn't answer 
a single question on a test.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.580
I was so frantic!

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:18.370
We've all been talking about 
moving forward positively.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.110
We like this place, too!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.960
Now, I'm going to change the subject a bit.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.550
You know of the terrorist attack in 
New York that was perpetrated by

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.280
people with terrifying powers, right?

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.970
Lisa, what did you think about 
the incident in Times Square?

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.620
This is inappropriate,

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.950
but it was as if the world of the comic 
books I always read had come to life,

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.740
so I was a little excited.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.080
<i>Last night in LA, thanks to 
the efforts of our blue hero,</i>

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.830
<i>I-Guy, a suspect who had taken 
hostages was apprehended.</i>

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:03.120
<i>The fact that he uses the culprit's 
capture as a form of entertainment</i>

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.240
Could you turn that off?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.210
<i>has garnered both supporters and naysayers, 
but he is getting a lot of attention.</i>

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.200
You finally spoke.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.110
So it's true that you have a car.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.500
But you didn't tell me it was so beat up.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.910
It's a hand-me-down from 
my dad. I can't help it.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.080
Your dad, eh?

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.240
Wouldn't that be a place you can go?

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.950
I guess the Reflected have 
nowhere to go, though.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.750
Hey, could you tell me

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.410
how we're Reflected, but still  
different from those monsters?

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.120
There are two types of Reflected.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:44.500
On that day three years ago, 
a black smoke covered the Earth.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.300
Then a green light broke through 
the smoke and made it disappear.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.480
But the smoke and light that 
hadn't mixed reached Earth.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.640
Many of the people who were hit 
by both lost their lives, but...

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:01.130
Those who survived became 
known as the Reflected.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:06.370
I believe the monsters that appeared 
at Times Square were hit by the smoke.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:11.490
Many of them are violent and antisocial,

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.000
and their appearances stand out.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:19.060
Many who were hit by the light gained powers

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:21.670
from some internal change... evidently.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:27.160
Was I hit by the light or the smoke?

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.640
I don't remember.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.380
I think that goes for most of us.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:14.120
I told her I was May's 
underclassman in high school,

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.770
but I wasn't able to learn anything from her.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:20.150
Actually, she ended up asking 
me various things about May.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:21.140
I felt bad.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.650
Even though Jennifer in New York is her cousin,

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.400
they'd only met as children.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:32.370
Apparently, this is the road 
May used to get to school.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:38.180
And that camera was the one 
that got the footage of him.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.510
Oh, no!

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.380
Are you all right?

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.330
I'm so sorry! Are you hurt?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.340
I'm fine. I'm sorry, I was going too fast.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:05.450
Let's go to the hospital. It wouldn't 
be good if you were hurt anywhere.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.430
Really, I'm...

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.110
No, this is my fault.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:26.110
I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.470
Oh, this isn't a big deal, either.

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:32.990
Thank goodness. I didn't know 
what I'd do if it were serious.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.010
That's right. What would you have done?

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.670
Dad...

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.480
I haven't seen you around here before.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.940
You're not from here, are you?

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.850
I'm a tourist. I was driving through.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.230
And an outsider like you 
hit her with your car?

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.670
My disabled daughter.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.640
I can "run" just fine!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.860
The wheelchair acts as my legs.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.940
I'm not disabled at all!

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.020
Lisa...

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:03.340
Also, don't call her an outsider.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.290
I've invited her to dinner.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:05.900
Huh?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:06.930
Let's go.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.830
Are you sure you don't need any help?

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.050
I'm fine. Please have a seat.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.290
I always eat dinner alone, 
so I'm happy to have you.

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.910
There's a funny story behind that one.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.450
When I was still inside my mother's tummy,

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.280
my dad thought I was going to be a boy,

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:45.990
and he dug up some toys 
from when he was little.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:51.110
So, for a while after I was born, 
they'd soothe me with that robot.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:53.710
You must be loved.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.670
Aren't you, too?

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.100
I'm not sure.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.860
I had a twin brother who died at birth.

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:08.760
Things might have been different... 
if my brother were here.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.840
Wow! You're a track athlete, Lisa?

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.840
I'm super fast.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.340
But you seem fast, too.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:19.940
Huh? No way!

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.950
Well, I'm quick to run away.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:32.160
I'd heard there was some troublesome 
woman who controlled metal.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.860
I guess that must be you.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.790
Which means cornering you 
here was a huge mistake...

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.650
You guys got what you wanted, didn't you?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.000
Or are you not done?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.320
I have no further use for you.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.330
But you played with me so much the other day!

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.120
I love this hero.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.260
He's a minor hero who can only fly...

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:40.210
But I wish I could fly freely 
through the sky, like Soar Man.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.030
Fly? Wow...

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.570
You're always pushing forward 
toward the future, huh?

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.800
Well, I mean, whether you're 
walking or in a wheelchair,

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.250
you're still bound by gravity.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:58.760
I want to abandon that weight 
and fly through the sky.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.800
Yeah.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.050
Someday, I want to stop running away, 
and push on toward the future.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.050
Like Soar Man?

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:09.620
Like you.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.620
She's my friend now!

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:19.890
Don't look at her weird just because 
she's not from here, Dad.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.240
All right. If she's your friend, 
we should give her a proper welcome.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.190
You're hungry, aren't you?

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.830
I didn't mean to frighten you.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:35.550
I only want to protect my daughter.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:36.210
I know.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.720
Three years ago...

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:45.420
A repeat drug offender 
I had previously arrested

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:48.580
came to our house after 
he was released from jail.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.550
And he took Lisa hostage.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:55.470
We determined the situation was 
volatile, and we made our move.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.130
Lisa!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.540
Are you all right, Lisa?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.250
Lisa was fine, but...

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.180
It was all my fault.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:34.510
Because I'm a cop, I get a lot of 
crazies who want revenge on me.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:39.110
I don't care what happens to me, 
but I'm going to protect Lisa.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:43.320
She's been in a wheelchair 
ever since she was born.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.720
I don't want anything else 
unfortunate to happen to her.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.490
But Lisa is...

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.080
I have my eye on all the filth in this town.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.630
But I can't keep my eye on 
every outsider, as well.

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:55.980
Lately,

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:59.960
we've had reports that some survivors 
of the Reflection are turning violent.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.430
That's why I was suspicious of you.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.500
Stop!

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:06.870
I've never thought of myself as unfortunate.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:09.600
Or that someone made me unfortunate.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:12.850
I want to know about many things...

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.250
I want to meet many people!

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.670
You don't know anything about the world!

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:17.950
That's why I—

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.760
You'll keep me tied down, right?

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.480
So I can't fly anywhere!

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:31.080
I think Lisa is a very strong girl.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:42.570
One of Wraith's subordinates?

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.160
But she didn't seem to be after us.

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:52.250
Lisa!

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:53.750
Lisa!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.430
Lisa...

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.380
Let me see your phone.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.610
Sorry, Debra,

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.690
but could you tell me where there's 
a lot of metal stockpiled in Dayton?

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:18.020
Who's Debra?

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.620
She and her crew are meddlesome and annoying,

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.680
but they're a hundred times 
more useful than you.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.060
Yeah, I owe you one.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:29.540
Let's go.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:45.560
Lisa!

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:48.770
Stay away from Lisa!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.280
Stop! Get your foot off her!

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:54.630
I hate to tell you this, 
but I don't feel a thing.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:58.480
But this rips out your father's heart.

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.800
You bastard!

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.480
Answer my question.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:06.030
Three years ago, she was hit, wasn't she?

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:07.530
What're you talking about?

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.230
Our wise master was able

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:13.220
to see through to her hidden powers,

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.600
and he sent me to get her.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:17.930
She's a Reflected, isn't she?

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:21.180
No! My daughter isn't a Reflected!

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:33.600
Looks like the father does feel pain.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:34.610
Dad!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:37.610
Now we can rip out the 
daughter's heart, too!

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.490
I don't know anything! 
I don't have any powers!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:46.990
You have a power. Now, remember that night...

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.620
You won't get away with this.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:54.370
Yes... Let your anger out. 
Release your power.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:58.160
No!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.770
Stop!

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.900
Putrid!

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:11.610
Don't worry. I'll be sure to extract 
that potential of yours.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:18.540
N-N-No!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.280
Stop...

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.830
Your power is unnecessary.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.350
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.630
Eleanor... What was that?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:06.500
Lisa, run!

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.110
Lisa!

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.970
Run... Run!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:29.040
Now, come into my chest!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.030
Lisa!

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:38.450
That's...

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:42.960
This is...

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.840
I'm not done yet. I'm still going to devour you!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.660
How dare you do that to my dad?!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.250
I se—

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.430
Not ba—

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:07.490
But my body—

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:21.230
Lisa...

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.650
I... I surrender.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:50.760
Dad!

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.700
Soar Man?

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:19.450
I...

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.130
Lisa,

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.890
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:47.390
But I couldn't believe it.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.940
No, I didn't want to believe it!

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:55.000
I'm sorry that I let this 
happen to your body.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.650
No. I got to fly.

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:02.870
It wasn't how I'd imagined it, 
but I became a hero!

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:04.870
Lisa...

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:07.810
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:11.170
All of this happened to you because of me.

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:12.550
It's all right.

00:22:13.070 --> 00:22:17.350
I'm pretty sure they won't give up on me.

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:19.880
That's why I'll...

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.540
If I stay here, something awful 
will happen to you again.

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.390
I can't stay here anymore.

00:22:25.850 --> 00:22:27.390
What are you saying?

00:22:27.390 --> 00:22:30.750
Also, Eleanor told me that

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:34.450
I'm always pushing forward 
toward the future.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.750
And I think she's right.

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:39.470
I want to know what these powers are...

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:42.180
And what I can do with them.

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:44.170
I want to see what I can do.

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:46.280
No! I won't let you go!

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:49.420
Dad!

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:50.560
Lisa...

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:01.430
Lisa...

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:11.080
Tell our master that we have 
made some progress.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Next Time 
New Orleans

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Narration: Stan Lee
